{"assertion":{"kind":"theoretical","text":"Erdős Problem #604: declared status 'open'. Formalized: no. Given $n$ distinct points $A\\subset\\mathbb{R}^2$ must there be a point $x\\in A$ such that\\[\\#\\{ d(x,y) : y \\in A\\} \\gg n^{1-o(1)}?\\]Or even $\\gg n/\\sqrt{\\log n}$? Current best: The best known bound is\\[\\gg n^{c-o(1)},\\]due to Katz and Tardos \\cite{KaTa04}, where\\[c=\\frac{48-14e}{55-16e}=0.864137\\cdots.\\]  References  [Er75f] Erd\\H{o}s, Paul, On some problems of elementary and combinatorial geometry. Prize: $500. Tags: distances, geometry."},"claim_id":"vcl_7b92e7d0824f8e9580ac7619b0582454d87237c0068c270a20cd31a39613dc49","conditions":[],"created_at":"2026-06-16T00:00:00Z","evidence":[],"extensions":{"vela.legacy-finding.v1":{"annotations":[],"attachments":[],"confidence":{"basis":"external catalogue record","extraction_confidence":1.0,"kind":"frontier_epistemic","method":"llm_initial","score":0.5},"flags":{"contested":false,"declining":false,"gap":false,"gravity_well":false,"negative_space":false,"retracted":false},"legacy_conditions":{"duration":null,"text":""},"legacy_evidence":{"evidence_spans":[],"method":"erdos_deep","model_system":"n/a","replicated":false,"replication_count":null,"type":"theoretical"},"legacy_links":[],"legacy_provenance":{"authors":[],"doi":null,"extraction":{"extracted_at":"","extractor_version":"","method":"database_import","model":null,"model_version":null},"review":null,"source_type":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:604","year":null},"previous_version":null,"source_schema":"https://vela.science/schema/finding-bundle/v0.10.0","source_version":1,"updated":null}},"imported_from":{"era":"finding_v0_10","object_id":"vf_860893aed23f1f18","object_root":"sha256:36a586a983deb5427892a6435d8eed5e26f91b1d16fb9c8be84abf12855fa065","predecessor_commit":"c236b4fdedb25e0d726e24e2780d50962e4844f7"},"provenance":[{"kind":"database_record","title":"erdos_deep:604"}],"relations":[],"revision":1,"schema":"vela.claim-record.v1"}